We say that an edge $e \in E(G)$ is \emph{satisfied} by $\pi$ if $\pi(e) \in E(H)$. We call $\pi$ an \emph{$\alpha$-isomorphism} for $G$ and $H$ if $\GI(G, H; \pi) \geq \alpha$, and we say $G$ and $H$ are \emph{$\alpha$-isomorphic} if $\GI(G, H) \geq \alpha$.
