    58	In an independent work, Codenotti, Schoenebeck, and Snook~\cite{CSS14} have shown a conclusion similar to our Theorem~\ref{thm:lasserre-gap}.  Their main result is that there are expander graphs $G$ and $H$ which are not isomorphic, but any SOS refutation of the statement ``$G$ and $H$ are isomorphic'' requires degree~$\Omega(n)$.  As in our work, their proof combines the Cai--F\"urer--Immerman construction with the Schoenebeck~\cite{Sch08} SOS/Lasserre lower bounds.
