   353	\begin{theorem} \label{thm:randomhypergraphwhp}
   354	   For any constant $k$, there exists constant $\kappa_k$, such that for $m=cn$ where $\kappa_k \leq c \leq \binom{n}{k}/\kappa_k^3$, $n$ large enough, if we set $\beta^* = \max\{\exp(-c/6),1/n\}$, with probability $(1 - n^{-15})$, for all $\beta : \beta^* \leq \beta \leq 1$, a random graph $H$ from the distribution $\calG^{(k)}_{n,m}$ is $(\beta,\beta/240)$-asymmetric. For $k=3$, $\kappa_3 = 10^{4}$ suffices.
