   127	A random \threexor instance with $n$ variables and $m$ equations is sampled by choosing $m$ unordered 3-tuples of variables from all possible ${n \choose 3}$ ones, and making each 3-tuple $(x_{j_1}, x_{j_2}, x_{j_3})$ into a \threexor constraint $x_{j_1} + x_{j_2} + x_{j_3} = b$ with an independent random $b \in \Z_2$. 
